      "content": {
        "quotes": [
          {
            "quote": "The assistant wrote the first draft of our test suite in an afternoon. We still reviewed every line, but it saved us a week of tedious work.",
            "person": "Jordan Ellis",
            "role": "Data Team Lead, Fernway",
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Fernway",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-8.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "quote": "New analysts ask it to explain the project instead of interrupting senior engineers, and they ship their first reviewed model in days rather than weeks. Onboarding used to be the slowest part of growing the team, and now it is one of the smoothest.",
            "person": "Mei Tanaka",
            "role": "Analytics Manager"
          },
          {
            "quote": "Debugging a failed run used to mean reading logs for an hour. Now the explanation and a proposed fix are waiting for me by the time I open my laptop, and most of the time the fix is right on the first try. When it is not, the explanation still points me to the right model, which is half the battle. It feels like pairing with a colleague who has read every file.",
            "person": "Daniel Brook",
            "role": "Senior Analytics Engineer"
          },
          {
            "quote": "We were cautious about AI in our codebase. The permissions model and audit log made it an easy approval for our security team.",
            "person": "Amara Nwosu",
            "role": "Director of Data Engineering"
          }
        ]
      },
